isory</a><a href="https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/blob/main/cves/2023/37xxx/CVE-2023-37393.json">Researcher credit</a></p></li></ul><p hidden="" id="disclosure-empty">No disclosures match. Try a product name or clear the filters.</p></div></details></div></div></section>
<section aria-labelledby="built-title" class="about-section sk-container about-surfaces" id="built"><p class="section-index">03 / Open source &amp; software</p><h2 id="built-title">Software I’ve built.</h2><p class="about-section-lede">Languages, local applications, and publishing tools from my current and earlier work.</p><div class="about-projects">
<article class="about-project about-project--lead"><div><span class="section-index">Language / Current focus</span><h3>Kujo</h3></div><div><p>A programming language and ecosystem for AI-native software. My work extends from the language and runtime into SDKs, agent workflows, package infrastructure, static publishing, evaluation, and developer tools.</p><p>These are connected engineering problems: defining what a program may do, making its state visible, and giving people a way to check the result.</p><div class="sk-cluster"><a class="sk-button" href="/projects/kujo/">Explore Kujo</a><a href="https://github.com/kujolang">Ecosystem source</a></div></div></article>
<article class="about-project"><div><span class="section-index">Local knowledge</span><h3>Strata</h3></div><div><p>A local-first Markdown notes application with keyboard navigation, an optional AI assistant, and CLI and HTTP interfaces. A place to preserve decisions and context alongside the work.</p><a href="https://github.com/robertdevore/strata">Strata source ↗</a></div></article>
<article class="about-project"><div><span class="section-index">Repository operations</span><h3>RepoRadar</h3></div><div><p>A local Git repository dashboard written in Kujo. It shows branch divergence, recent commits, file changes, and repository health in one place.</p><a href="https://github.com/robertdevore/reporadar">RepoRadar source ↗</a></div></article>
<article class="about-project"><div><span class="section-index">Version-controlled content</span><h3>DB Version Control</h3></div><div><p>A WordPress plugin that saves content as JSON files for Git workflows. I created the project; WebDevStudios now maintains it.</p><a href="https://github.com/WebDevStudios/db-version-control">DB Version Control source ↗</a></div></article>
<article class="about-project"><div><span class="section-index">Desktop utilities</span><h3>Snips</h3></div><div><p>A local-first macOS text expander with an Electron library, SQLite storage, and a native Swift helper for expanding abbreviations across applications.</p><a href="https://github.com/robertdevore/snips">Snips source ↗</a></div></article>
<article class="about-project"><div><span class="section-index">Content portability</span><h3>Markdown Exporter</h3></div><div><p>A WordPress plugin for exporting posts, pages, and custom content types into Markdown. A practical bridge between a publishing platform and files you can version, move, and reuse.</p><a href="https://github.com/robertdevore/markdown-exporter-for-wordpress">Markdown Exporter source ↗</a></div></article></div><p class="about-source-note">Open source also means making room for the next maintainer. In 2025, <a href="/grateful-to-see-21-of-my-wordpress-plugins-live-on-at-webdevstudios/">WebDevStudios adopted 20 of my WordPress plugins</a>. <a href="/projects/">Explore more of my software</a>.</p></section>
<section aria-labelledby="writing-title" class="about-learning" id="writing"><div class="sk-container about-editorial"><div><p class="section-index">04 / Writing, education &amp; community</p><h2 id="writing-title">Build it.<br/>Understand it.<br/>Explain it.</h2><p class="about-section-lede">Writing helps me explain how things work and gives others a way to build on what I’ve learned.</p><a class="sk-button" href="/blog/">Read the field notes</a></div><div class="about-prose"><p>I publish technical guides, project histories, release notes, and essays about the people and decisions behind software. The archive connects years of PHP and WordPress work with current language, tooling, and AI engineering projects.</p><aside aria-labelledby="press-title" class="about-press" data-no-scramble=""><p class="section-index">Coverage &amp; interviews</p><h3 id="press-title">Featured press</h3><ul class="about-reading"><li><a href="https://www.searchenginejournal.com/wordpress-developer-publishes-code-to-block-mullenwegs-web-hosting-clients/536427/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><strong>Search Engine Journal</strong><span>Reporting on my WordPress code · 2024</span><span class="about-press-action">Read the coverage ↗</span></a></li><li><a href="https://withinwp.com/newsletter/faster-woo-and-new-and-improved-generateblocks-wpgraphql/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><strong>Within WP</strong><span>AI-Powered Patterns plugin mention · 2025</span><span class="about-press-action">Read the newsletter ↗</span></a></li><li><a href="https://thewpminute.com/open-source-saved-my-life/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><strong>The WP Minute</strong><span>“Open Source Saved My Life” · Interview, 2025</span><span class="about-press-action">Listen to the interview ↗</span></a></li><li><a href="https://wptavern.com/wp-dispensary-offers-a-complete-marijuana-menu-solution-for-wordpress" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><strong>WP Tavern</strong><span>Coverage of WP Dispensary · 2016</span><span class="about-press-action">Read the coverage ↗</span></a></li></ul></aside><h3>Independent courses</h3><p>My courses combine lessons with practical exercises to help you learn by building.</p><ul class="about-course-links"><li><a href="https://typescript.robertdevore.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">TypeScript</a></li><li><a href="https://rust.robertdevore.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Rust</a></li><li><a href="https://python.robertdevore.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Python</a></li><li><a href="https://kujo.robertdevore.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Kujo</a></li><li><a href="https://cpc.robertdevore.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">CPC study course</a></li><li><a href="https://edgeacademy.robertdevore.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Edge Academy</a></li></ul><p class="about-source-note">Independent educational resources. CPC is not affiliated with AAPC and awards no certification; Edge Academy is not affiliated with Cloudflare. <a href="/courses/">Browse the course catalog</a>.</p></div></div></section>
<section aria-labelledby="approach-title" class="about-section sk-container about-editorial" id="approach"><div><p class="section-index">05 / Engineering principles</p><h2 id="approach-title">Leave the system<br/>easier to understand.</h2></div><dl class="about-principles"><div><dt>Make the boundaries explicit.</dt><dd>Know what an input can affect, which permissions an action needs, and where a person should stay in control.</dd></div><div><dt>Prefer evidence to assumptions.</dt><dd>Keep the inputs, checks, and results close enough that someone else can reproduce the work.</dd></div><div><dt>Choose clarity that lasts.</dt><dd>A smaller, understandable system is easier to secure and maintain. Documentation and useful errors belong in the design.</dd></div><div><dt>Build for the next person.</dt><dd>Good interfaces, open source, and honest handoffs help work remain useful after its original author moves on.</dd></div></dl></section>
<section aria-labelledby="connect-title" class="about-closing"><div class="sk-container"><p class="section-index">06 / Connect</p><h2 id="connect-title">Have a problem worth thinking through?</h2><p>I’m interested in working with engineering teams, open-source contributors, and security researchers on difficult software problems. If that sounds like your work, let’s talk.</p><div class="sk-cluster"><a class="sk-button" href="/contact/">Get in touch</a><a href="https://github.com/robertdevore">Find me on GitHub ↗</a></div></div></section>
</main>
